This is correct behavior.

|Wiz mode, and I probed the dog every time I made one.  The only way to avoid
|saying the ring caused his attack would ...

You don't have to avoid saying it.  Go ahead...say it.  You are right!

I think it's easy to misunderstand postings when a rabid flame-fest is
going on.  People seem to reply to each other without fully understanding
the quoted articles.  I think that the major source of confusion in the
original exchange was the assumptions of whether or not a ring of
conflict was being worn.

If you are not wearing a ring of conflict, your dog will choose for
himself who he will or will not fight (based on monster levels).  If
you are wearing a ring of conflict, you are FORCING your dog to fight,
just the same as you force other monsters to fight.

